{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'litehive report --verdict reject --role reviewer --step accepting --message \"EXPECTED behavior: For implementing-stage fanout, if any launched SWE worker is interrupted or fails, the task should remain recoverable at the same stage (`implementing`) with persisted per-worker context, and focused tests should cover both interruption and failure behavior in addition to success/live-state/observability. OBSERVED behavior: Interrupted fanout is recoverable and the new multi-worker persistence/observability tests pass, but ordinary worker failure is not recoverable. `_aggregate_parallel_reports()` can return `fail` for implementing fanout, and `TaskExecutionRunner` has no (`implementing`, `fail`) route, so the task is marked `flagged` instead of being re-queued/recoverable at `implementing`. In reproduction, the run ends with `final_status=flagged`, `task_status=flagged`, `pipeline_status=implementing`, `runtime_last_outcome_kind=flagged`, while `runtime.subagent_states` contains both completed and failed workers. Steps to reproduce: run `uv run pytest -q tests/test_runner_workflow.py -k '\"'fans_out_parallel_workers_within_implementing_stage or keeps_interrupted_fanout_task_recoverable'\"'`, `uv run pytest -q tests/test_tasks_and_subagents.py -k persists_multiple_live_worker_states`, and `uv run pytest -q tests/test_observability_and_status.py -k render_task_summary_and_snapshot_include_multiple_active_subagents` to confirm the covered paths pass; then run the following reproduction script to demonstrate the gap: `uv run python - <<'\"'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nimport tempfile\\\\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\\\\nfrom litehive.runtime import run_task\\\\nfrom litehive.models import RuntimeSubagentState, SubagentRef\\\\nfrom litehive import tasks as tasks_module\\\\nfrom litehive.config import ensure_workspace\\\\nfrom litehive.tasks import create_task\\\\nfrom litehive.subagents import EngineFailure, SubagentResult\\\\nfrom litehive.external_cli import CLIExecutionResult\\\\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\\\\n    root = Path(tmp)\\\\n    ensure_workspace(root)\\\\n    task = create_task(root, title='Failed fanout', acceptance_criteria=['recoverable'], auto_commit=False)\\\\n    task.pipeline_status = 'implementing'\\\\n    task.plan = ['slice one', 'slice two']\\\\n    tasks_module.save_task(root, task)\\\\n    def fake_run(self, current_task, role, engine_name, prompt, model=None, max_turns=None, resume_session_id=None, worker_key=None, assignment=''):\\\\n        ref = SubagentRef(id=f'SA-{worker_key}', role='swe', engine=engine_name, status='running', path=f'subagents/{worker_key}-swe', worker_key=worker_key, assignment=assignment)\\\\n        if all(existing.id \"'!= ref.id for existing in current_task.subagents):'\"\\\\n            current_task.subagents.append(ref)\\\\n        tasks_module._upsert_runtime_subagent_state(current_task, RuntimeSubagentState(id=ref.id, role=ref.role, engine=ref.engine, status='running', path=ref.path, worker_key=ref.worker_key, assignment=ref.assignment, started_at='2026-04-04T10:00:00+00:00', updated_at='2026-04-04T10:00:01+00:00'))\\\\n        tasks_module._refresh_runtime_subagent_views(current_task)\\\\n        if worker_key == 'worker-02':\\\\n            ref.status = 'failed'\\\\n            tasks_module._upsert_runtime_subagent_state(current_task, RuntimeSubagentState(id=ref.id, role=ref.role, engine=ref.engine, status='failed', path=ref.path, worker_key=ref.worker_key, assignment=ref.assignment, started_at='2026-04-04T10:00:00+00:00', updated_at='2026-04-04T10:00:02+00:00', completed_at='2026-04-04T10:00:02+00:00', exit_code=1, transcript_snippet='worker failed'))\\\\n            tasks_module._refresh_runtime_subagent_views(current_task)\\\\n            return SubagentResult(ref=ref, execution=CLIExecutionResult(adapter='codex', argv=('codex',), cwd=root, exit_code=1, stdout='VERDICT: FAIL\\\\\\\\nSUMMARY: worker failed\\\\\\\\n', stderr='boom', pid=1234), transcript='VERDICT: FAIL\\\\\\\\nSUMMARY: worker failed\\\\\\\\n', exit_code=1, failure=EngineFailure(kind='engine_error', reason='boom'))\\\\n        ref.status = 'completed'\\\\n        tasks_module._upsert_runtime_subagent_state(current_task, RuntimeSubagentState(id=ref.id, role=ref.role, engine=ref.engine, status='completed', path=ref.path, worker_key=ref.worker_key, assignment=ref.assignment, started_at='2026-04-04T10:00:00+00:00', updated_at='2026-04-04T10:00:02+00:00', completed_at='2026-04-04T10:00:02+00:00', exit_code=0, transcript_snippet='worker complete'))\\\\n        tasks_module._refresh_runtime_subagent_views(current_task)\\\\n        return SubagentResult(ref=ref, execution=CLIExecutionResult(adapter='codex', argv=('codex',), cwd=root, exit_code=0, stdout='VERDICT: PASS\\\\\\\\nSUMMARY: worker complete\\\\\\\\n', stderr='', pid=1233), transcript='VERDICT: PASS\\\\\\\\nSUMMARY: worker complete\\\\\\\\n', exit_code=0, failure=None)\\\\n    with patch('litehive.runtime.SubagentManager.run', new=fake_run):\\\\n        summary = run_task(root, task)\\\\n    refreshed = tasks_module.require_task(root, task.id)\\\\n    print(summary.result.final_status, refreshed.status, refreshed.pipeline_status, refreshed.runtime.last_outcome.kind)\\\\nPY\"'` -> observed output `flagged flagged implementing flagged`. Acceptance criteria status: criterion 1 is met for successful fanout waiting semantics; criterion 2 is met for persisted live per-worker state; criterion 3 is met for status/web observability of multiple workers; criterion 4 is only partially met because interruption is recoverable but failed fanout is not; criterion 5 is not fully met because there is no focused test covering failed fanout behavior.\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
